{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm","id":1487162,"title":"Vampirism as a positive- subverting the core premise of VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-20T04:17:36-07:00","id":1487162,"title":"Vampirism as a positive- subverting the core premise of VTM","content":"I've been thinking a lot about how people actually play vtm a lot lately and the potential disconnect with play and core themes. i was reading another thread on Reddit (<a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comments/vzjw2d/my_beautiful_pair_of_blood_brothers_blaire/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.reddit.com/r/vtm/comment...others_blaire/</a>) and as I explored it and other similar threads on the subject I noticed the consistent a lot of PC characters seems to either enjoy the vampiric condition or enjoy interesting fulfilling lives rather than reveling in their own misery. With this in mind I'm wondering how many people play vtm as it's supposed to be played, now I'm not talking about simply exploring different aspect such a political games or say blade style streets battles, I mean &quot;I really like being a vampire. I don't want to be human&quot; full stop no &quot;woe is me I labour under this terrible curse but lack conviction to walk into the sun&quot; no &quot;I'm so horribly messed up I'm unaware of my own desolation&quot;. Considering v5 tries to mechanically enforce existential horror and I'm still seeing this come up, i think it's certainly an ongoing issue which is worth considering even if we disregard mary sues or weird personal fantasies.<br /> <br /> <br /> -thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-20-2022, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T04:25:18-07:00","id":1487167,"title":"","content":"I think vampirism should have horrifying moments but as a Storyteller, I've always encouraged the view that every vampire has some acceptance of their condition.<br /> <br /> And at least something they absolutely love about it.<br /> <br /> * Being able to pick up attractive partners.<br /> * The feeling of invulnerability.<br /> * The ability to abuse people who abused you in life.<br /> * Literal superpowers.<br /> * Immortality.<br /> * Immunity to disease.<br /> * The ability to appreciate things with super-senses.<br /> * People you care about in the afterlife like your coterie or progeny/sire. I do encourage vampires to fall in love.<br /> <br /> And of course the thing that motivates all vampires: blood.<br /> <br /> Its sex and drugs every night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T05:41:45-07:00","id":1487179,"title":"","content":"I mean, I think about the things that give a human's life fulfillment. Meaningful long term relationships and a long term purpose that spans both day to day as well as over many years. <br /> <br /> Vampires are largely cut off from the former by virtue of their immorality, and many of the purposes humans derive fulfillment from are cut off from them via the Masquerade and inability to procreate. <br /> <br /> While I think it's entirely possible to experience a joyful, fulfilling existence as a Vampire, I think it's something the vampire must consciously choose every night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T06:08:47-07:00","id":1487180,"title":"","content":"Requiem does something similar, it does have personal horror as one of the core aspects but it's outlook on vampirism is less &quot;woe me I'm a loathsome creature of the night&quot; and more like &quot;Ok sugar, you are a blood sucking immortal with a sun allergy, a short but manageable temper, cool powers and infinite possibilities, what are you going to do about it?&quot;, it does point out that vampirism is a curse but doesn't dwell too much on it, the positives in general, far outweight the negatives and the beast is nowhere near the time bomb it is in masquerade (although it's definitely going to ruin your night if you give in too much).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T06:10:33-07:00","id":1487181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487167#post1487167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think vampirism should have horrifying moments but as a Storyteller, I've always encouraged the view that every vampire has some acceptance of their condition.<br /> <br /> And at least something they absolutely love about it.<br /> <br /> * Being able to pick up attractive partners.<br /> * The feeling of invulnerability.<br /> * The ability to abuse people who abused you in life.<br /> * Literal superpowers.<br /> * Immortality.<br /> * Immunity to disease.<br /> * The ability to appreciate things with super-senses.<br /> * People you care about in the afterlife like your coterie or progeny/sire. I do encourage vampires to fall in love.<br /> <br /> And of course the thing that motivates all vampires: blood.<br /> <br /> Its sex and drugs every night.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On a sidenote, I really wish masquerade made up it's goddamn mind on the vamps &quot;supersenses&quot; because, aside from auspex and protean, vamps have the exact same sensory range as humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T06:59:07-07:00","id":1487183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Newb95</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487181#post1487181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On a sidenote, I really wish masquerade made up it's goddamn mind on the vamps &quot;supersenses&quot; because, aside from auspex and protean, vamps have the exact same sensory range as humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's always gotten on my nerves as well, especially the not being able to see in the dark as a default racial thing. They fixed it in Requiem, then went right back to it in V5. Vampires should not be stumbling around in the dark like Leslie Nelson's goofy comedy Dracula.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:00:29-07:00","id":1487185,"title":"","content":"Really, other than having to sleep during the day, having a Beast and having to drink blood, being a vampire isn't that bad. Especially when you factor in the immortality, magical powers and everything else. Sure, I get that it's supposed to be a curse and all that, but there's a lot of vampires who enjoy their condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:50:49-07:00","id":1487192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487185#post1487185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, other than having to sleep during the day, having a Beast and having to drink blood, being a vampire isn't that bad. Especially when you factor in the immortality, magical powers and everything else. Sure, I get that it's supposed to be a curse and all that, but there's a lot of vampires who enjoy their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What makes vampire's unlives shitty in masquerade (and to a lesser extent requiem) is the utterly abominable enviroment they live in, not only you are undead and in need of blood everyday but you also have to deal with a feudal society of immortal monsters who could crush you like an insect the second you prove to be an inconvenience to them, if vamps didn't need to deal with the Camarilla, the Anarchs and the Sabbat, their unlives would be MUCH easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27142-newb95","name":"Newb95","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:57:53-07:00","id":1487194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487185#post1487185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, other than having to sleep during the day, having a Beast and having to drink blood, being a vampire isn't that bad. Especially when you factor in the immortality, magical powers and everything else. Sure, I get that it's supposed to be a curse and all that, but there's a lot of vampires who enjoy their condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because this is a fiction.<br /> <br /> For example, when we go see a movie, it is a cathartic experience when the hero finally &quot;oomps&quot; the bad guy. It gives a sense of relief, justice served, and we derive pleasure from that tiny spot of sadism that we all posses inside our hearts but we keep repressed and pretend not to have it.<br /> <br /> That's a fiction, a &quot;controlled simulation&quot; if you, in a safe environment.<br /> <br /> I never had to kill anybody, thanks the heavens, Im not criminal, no police, no soldier, nor a stone age H sapiens fighting for my survival. I dont know exactly how it would feel having to look the face of desperation in somebody else's eyes, and then pulling the trigger. But Im sure it wouldnt be the same experience we get from the pleasure of seeing the villain getting killed in a movie.<br /> <br /> Experiencing a sensation in our own skin is different from running mental simulations of hypothetical scenarios.<br /> <br /> Being a vampire sounds awesome for all those reasons - feeling like an immortal super hero - but that's only because we &quot;experience&quot; it only as a mental simulation. Which is why we can make all those hypotheticals about how &quot;awesome&quot; it would be.<br /> <br /> But in truth, it wouldnt be awesome, it would be terrible. First, you would be disconnected from the light. You may think that's trivial, but just you try living exclusively at night without even seeing the light of the day. That's a super depressive way to live - of that I do have some personal experience (which is gladly in the past).<br /> <br /> Second, the total disconnection from the rest of the world. Now, some people are more reserved, even loners, and may think this is no big deal, but in fact it is. Because a vampire aint just disconnected from other normal people, they are disconnected from human condition. And there's only 2 ways a vampire can view humans after their embrace:<br /> - Mortals are beneath me, Im so far beyond the fragile cattle;<br /> Or<br /> - Mortals are innocent sheep which I must tend to because they cand defend themselves<br /> <br /> Thus, vampires will ALWAYS have a condescending view towards other humans, and a patronizing attitute. It's inevitable due to their condition.<br /> <br /> That means that a vampire will be constantly be surrounded by creatures who no longer are of their kind, and who are just simply... Inferior. The cop stopping you in the traffic, he's either a petulant child who have no idea who he is dealing with, or a poor innocent child that has no idea the dangerous world he lives in.<br /> <br /> All of a sudden, mortal considerations become utterly banal. You, after all, have more pressing matters to attend than the frivolous day to day struggles of the innocent sheep.<br /> <br /> Immortality is also another curse. Even without all the sun allergy and blood drinking, immortality is still a heavy burden. Sure it may seem fun at the beggining. But just imagine, day in and day out, same old same old... Forever. Sure, let's break the routine a bit today. And tomorrow. And the day after... And after a while, &quot;breaking the routine&quot; becomes the new boring and emotionless routine.<br /> <br /> No, vampirism is only &quot;cool&quot; when we consider it for a small entertainment game.<br /> <br /> If vampirism was real, it would be a freaking nightmare.<br /> <br /> Edit: and that's in my humble opinion is why so many people play VTM in the &quot;cool aspects&quot; of vampirism, and how awesome it is and what not, because we dont experience it, we experience only the mental simulations that design inside our heads, thus it's perfectly vallid to play in such a manner, but it wouldnt reflect reality, at least in the way I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 07-20-2022, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T08:13:43-07:00","id":1487195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487194#post1487194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in truth, it wouldnt be awesome, it would be terrible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> The truth still is this is fiction. The horror, the curse, the disconnect, they're tropes.<br /> <br /> We don't know what being a vampire would be like. We don't know what being immortal would be like. We have genre assumptions and traditions, not data. Indeed, a lot of those assumptions have no basis or even contradicts what little actual science can extrapolate from our current knowledge on human Psychology and Neurology.<br /> <br /> Sure, being cut from the light of day is horrible for a human, because it is horrible for a human brain. A vampire doe not have a human brain even if they have a human(-ish) mind, because vital or not to their anatomies, the organ is as dead and shriveled as every other in a vampire's internal body. Also, not everyone reacts to this in the same way, or under the same conditions.<br /> <br /> Everything about vampires is fiction. And everything about RPGs is also fiction. The idea that playing them in a given way is more realistic is pure pretension, and the idea that realism is a superior mode of play in any way is pure snobbery. Not that anyone in particular is pretentious or snob just by thinking those very popular and repeated ideas are true.<br /> <br /> But no. Just no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T09:38:28-07:00","id":1487203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487195#post1487195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope.<br /> <br /> The truth still is this is fiction. The horror, the curse, the disconnect, they're tropes.<br /> <br /> We don't know what being a vampire would be like. We don't know what being immortal would be like. We have genre assumptions and traditions, not data. Indeed, a lot of those assumptions have no basis or even contradicts what little actual science can extrapolate from our current knowledge on human Psychology and Neurology.<br /> <br /> Sure, being cut from the light of day is horrible for a human, because it is horrible for a human brain. A vampire doe not have a human brain even if they have a human(-ish) mind, because vital or not to their anatomies, the organ is as dead and shriveled as every other in a vampire's internal body. Also, not everyone reacts to this in the same way, or under the same conditions.<br /> <br /> Everything about vampires is fiction. And everything about RPGs is also fiction. The idea that playing them in a given way is more realistic is pure pretension, and the idea that realism is a superior mode of play in any way is pure snobbery. Not that anyone in particular is pretentious or snob just by thinking those very popular and repeated ideas are true.<br /> <br /> But no. Just no.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. Indeed such is the case. I stand corrected. Vampires are indeed (most probably?) a fiction, thus no &quot;realistic&quot; view is possible.<br /> <br /> So, let me rephrase it all: in my opinion, the vampiric condition is a terrible curse; that's however just as subjective of an interpretation as any others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:09:16-07:00","id":1487226,"title":"","content":"Well the setting is one of horror of becoming slowly but surely becoming a monster that only has a passing resemblence to what you once were. So there is not much positives in the end and my character driving desire is making the best of a bad situation that he wouldn't wish upon his worst enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T12:36:33-07:00","id":1487231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487183#post1487183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, that's always gotten on my nerves as well, especially the not being able to see in the dark as a default racial thing. They fixed it in Requiem, then went right back to it in V5. Vampires should not be stumbling around in the dark like Leslie Nelson's goofy comedy Dracula.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember to move your coffin away from the chandelier, and beware of daymares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T13:03:16-07:00","id":1487238,"title":"","content":"No vampire is ever further from suicide than the next sunrise. If their condition were genuinely intolerable, none of them would tolerate it.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, suicide <i>is </i>in fact the single biggest cause of Final Death among vampires under a hundred, despite the Second Inquisition's best efforts. With two flashpoints - immediately after the Embrace, and when the last person they knew in their mortal lives dies of old age.<br /> <br /> I don't play it as a positive so much as a condition with horrific aspects which nonetheless has (for some) sufficient compensations to make it endurable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/100-jezmiller","name":"JezMiller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T13:09:18-07:00","id":1487240,"title":"","content":"Most of my VtM characters have enjoyed the glamorous and romantic aspects of being a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:10:26-07:00","id":1487259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JezMiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487238#post1487238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No vampire is ever further from suicide than the next sunrise. If their condition were genuinely intolerable, none of them would tolerate it.<br /> <br /> In my headcanon, suicide <i>is </i>in fact the single biggest cause of Final Death among vampires under a hundred, despite the Second Inquisition's best efforts. With two flashpoints - immediately after the Embrace, and when the last person they knew in their mortal lives dies of old age.<br /> <br /> I don't play it as a positive so much as a condition with horrific aspects which nonetheless has (for some) sufficient compensations to make it endurable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt it impossible for them to do it thou? I always thought that the beast doesnt allow you to simply take a sun bath, or jumping into a fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:16:15-07:00","id":1487260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487259#post1487259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isnt it impossible for them to do it thou? I always thought that the beast doesnt allow you to simply take a sun bath, or jumping into a fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The terror frenzy is how it TRIES to keep you from suicide.<br /> <br /> But if you're in the middle of central park, well, not much problem with it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:43:26-07:00","id":1487262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487260#post1487260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The terror frenzy is how it TRIES to keep you from suicide.<br /> <br /> But if you're in the middle of central park, well, not much problem with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, suicide aint so easy to do. I hate call it that way, but it takes &quot;courage&quot;, or an excessive amount of desperation in a fleeting moment. Even high depression aint enough for it - in fact, in most cases where a person is in the deepest depression, it's actually harder to attempt suicide, because the person simply lacks the drive, the energy, the impulse to do it, because suicide is on most of the cases a matter of a few seconds of impulse. Which is why when a depressive person starts treatment with anti depressives, it must be closely watched in the first few weeks, exactly because the medicine may actually give her that boost of energy that the person requires to have that 1 second for the impusive jump.<br /> <br /> It wouldnt be impossible for vampires to spend centuries wishing to die, but not having the necessary drive to do it - althought this would be a hell on Earth for such poor creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T15:49:34-07:00","id":1487266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487262#post1487262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, suicide aint so easy to do. I hate call it that way, but it takes &quot;courage&quot;, or an excessive amount of desperation in a fleeting moment. Even high depression aint enough for it - in fact, in most cases where a person is in the deepest depression, it's actually harder to attempt suicide, because the person simply lacks the drive, the energy, the impulse to do it, because suicide is on most of the cases a matter of a few seconds of impulse. Which is why when a depressive person starts treatment with anti depressives, it must be closely watched in the first few weeks, exactly because the medicine may actually give her that boost of energy that the person requires to have that 1 second for the impusive jump.<br /> <br /> It wouldnt be impossible for vampires to spend centuries wishing to die, but not having the necessary drive to do it - althought this would be a hell on Earth for such poor creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>THE WITCHER basically had a scene saying that suicide takes a great deal of will but little skill when the protagonist (Ciri, not Geralt) tries it.<br /> <br /> In the case of suicide by sunlight, I assume sunlight is the easiest way for a vampire to do it because its the hardest thing to escape if you plan ahead.<br /> <br /> So I think a lot of vampires do commit suicide by sunbath but I also believe there's more failed attempts than successes because most people, especially vampires, don't WANT to do it anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T16:06:27-07:00","id":1487268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487266#post1487266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> THE WITCHER basically had a scene saying that suicide takes a great deal of will but little skill when the protagonist (Ciri, not Geralt) tries it.<br /> <br /> In the case of suicide by sunlight, I assume sunlight is the easiest way for a vampire to do it because its the hardest thing to escape if you plan ahead.<br /> <br /> So I think a lot of vampires do commit suicide by sunbath but I also believe there's more failed attempts than successes because most people, especially vampires, don't WANT to do it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I went throw several periods of severe apathy in my life were I didnt live at all, I would just do things mechanically, but dead inside. Eating, sleeping, bathing, all that done mechanically, completely emotionless, and not caring at all. I didnt care to die at all to die, on my worse days I would beg for it to happen, but indeed I lacked the will to do it, I lacked the energy to even try. I know the feeling from personal experience sadly, which is why I said it. Suicide aint so easy, even for those that are living under the most despair and with no hope.<br /> <br /> But I did have a friend, my best friend, who commited suicide. More than 20 years ago. In a moment of impulsiveness, he just jumped out of the window, out of the blue. I knew he was depressive too, just as Im sure he knew I was. The cynism and the fake smile and false happiness, it's easy to spot on one another. I still dream with him sometimes, and wish I could destroy his dumb ass for what he's done.<br /> <br /> Im better now, I have a beautiful wife and 3 gorgeous kids who are the light of my life, despite some fleeting moments of apathy, but never as severe as I had before. But I can tell you, a person can exist as a zombie, a literal undead, alive just on the outside, but absolutely dead on the inside. I wouldnt find it weird for a vampire spending centuries wishing for death, but unable to embrace it - and the longer it spends on that condition, the less unlikely it would be for such a vampire to entertain the notion.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's how I view most of the elders: completely dead inside, emontionless creatures uncapable of feeling anything, which is why they dedicate themselves to their political games and machinations, as coping mechanisms. And that's why such an existance would be so abhorrent to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T16:24:14-07:00","id":1487271,"title":"","content":"RPGs are for stepping out of your shoes and into someone else's for a play session so you can unplug from your life and explore alternatives with relatively no consequences. But this also means that any given RPG means vastly different things to each player.<br /> <br /> VtM to a teenager usually embodies those feelings of angst, isolation, raging inner feelings, all consuming/obsessive love, and the various high school drama that goes along with that mountain of emotional &amp; psychological baggage. Horror at this point in life is raging all over the place, but not understanding the collateral damage you cause to those around you.<br /> <br /> VtM to a young adult (mid 20s to early 30s) is probably a way to get back to a time when they didn't have the responsibilities that they endure now. The PCs have career paths that are fun, they party every night, they travel and go on adventures. Basically, everything a 9 to 5 eternal wage slave dreams of, will never get, and can only labor under massive amounts of financial debt. The horror of this point of life is that the wage slave existence is eternal, you will never be rested, you will never have a better life, and your chances at finding a mate are dwindling by the year.<br /> <br /> VtM for a mature adult (mid 30s to 40s) can go in one of two ways. The first is that the player is trying to experience something from an earlier time in their life. Be it the carefree days of being a teenager or being in their 20s before their bodies started breaking down on them. The second path is that the player is wanting to explore variations on a theme, in that they have made it in life and as such understand what is important and what isn't, but they want to see how that understanding of the world changes with different skill sets and goals. The horror of this stage is one of &quot;what's next?&quot; in that if you have survived and managed to escape the rat race, what else is there in life. You have been through enough things that what others see as important; you see as a fad. What others claim is a disability; you merely see as a weakness they need to learn to overcome. But the worst of all is that in the end; you just don't care.<br /> <br /> IMHO this is one of the main reasons Elder Vampires are so poorly written in general. When you become a vampire, you are now ageless, immune to disease, have magical powers, and are separated from mortal society enough to fulfil any base desire on a nightly basis. Once you have secured an income source, a high security haven or two, and a safe source of blood, you have nothing left to set up. Everything else after that point is merely something you do for amusement or in the cases of more enlightened individuals, to improve oneself. Instead, Elders are written and used as plot points rather than mature fleshed out characters.<br /> <br /> Just because a game claims to be one thing or another, doesn't mean that the individual playing it would perceive the situation as such. If a Lawful Good Paladin in D&amp;D can slaughter their way through non-believers and have a good nights sleep, then a Vampire who simply accepts their unlife and lets go of trivial things, can be just as happy. Then again there just are those individuals who psychologically are comfortable in harsher situations than others. What some consider Horror, they would consider a normal day.<br /> <br /> In conclusion I have run vampire games that ranged from goofy comedy to players needing to do some IRL thinking because they went to very dark places, and everything in between. But as long as the group had a good time, that's all that mattered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T16:27:48-07:00","id":1487272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487268#post1487268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I went throw several periods of severe apathy in my life were I didnt live at all, I would just do things mechanically, but dead inside. Eating, sleeping, bathing, all that done mechanically, completely emotionless, and not caring at all. I didnt care to die at all to die, on my worse days I would beg for it to happen, but indeed I lacked the will to do it, I lacked the energy to even try. I know the feeling from personal experience sadly, which is why I said it. Suicide aint so easy, even for those that are living under the most despair and with no hope.<br /> <br /> But I did have a friend, my best friend, who commited suicide. More than 20 years ago. In a moment of impulsiveness, he just jumped out of the window, out of the blue. I knew he was depressive too, just as Im sure he knew I was. The cynism and the fake smile and false happiness, it's easy to spot on one another. I still dream with him sometimes, and wish I could destroy his dumb ass for what he's done.<br /> <br /> Im better now, I have a beautiful wife and 3 gorgeous kids who are the light of my life, despite some fleeting moments of apathy, but never as severe as I had before. But I can tell you, a person can exist as a zombie, a literal undead, alive just on the outside, but absolutely dead on the inside. I wouldnt find it weird for a vampire spending centuries wishing for death, but unable to embrace it - and the longer it spends on that condition, the less unlikely it would be for such a vampire to entertain the notion.<br /> <br /> In fact, that's how I view most of the elders: completely dead inside, emontionless creatures uncapable of feeling anything, which is why they dedicate themselves to their political games and machinations, as coping mechanisms. And that's why such an existance would be so abhorrent to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, unfortunately I have immediate family members who have attempted suicides and some who have succeeded.<br /> <br /> It's a horrifically sensitive topic and should be treated with the utmost care in game.<br /> <br /> It shouldn't be used flippantly like they did in ANARCH.<br /> <br /> (And no, there's no &quot;caveat&quot; like, &quot;But they did do..&quot;)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:03:02-07:00","id":1487278,"title":"","content":"There are several reasons why suicide is a heavy topic, and usually conversations about vampires and suicide aren't very constructive in the middle of arguments if &quot;they would&quot; or, worse, &quot;they should&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the bottom line to it is that it isn't a normal action in any sense. It isn't strength and it isn't weakness, it isn't courage, it isn't cowardice. It is too easy, both for those who are sick and think about it and for those who don't, to imagine or say shit about it. The reality of it is messy, painful and desperate in a level most people cannot grasp even when in its actual grasp.<br /> <br /> Vampires possibly commit suicide. If you feel confident to deal with this topic with your group, go for it. If you're not sure, or worse, if you have a personal <i>opinion</i> on it and wants to <i>show your headcanon on suicide</i> to people you're not sure about... <b><u>JUST DON'T</u></b>. And it isn't necessarily a big cause of deaths among them, either, no matter how bleak you think their existence is.<br /> <br /> Yet, the point of the thread is that their existence isn't necessarily bleak. Because the very reasons why we think it would be may not be there to begin with. We can form deep connections to people we knew just a few years ago, and cope without a problem with losing old connections as time goes on and they become sweet memories. I've lost families, friends and pets through my life, yet I keep making friends, commemorating births and adopting puppies that I know will grow old and die.<br /> <br /> It isn't hard to think of a character that savors life and contributes to society just as anyone could being a mortal, once we takes in the proposed subversion of the premise and stop thinking this character in a Punk-Gothic context (even if still with a Punk-Gothic aesthetic). Actually, with a bit more effort we can have such a character even in the middle of a more &quot;regular&quot; chronicle, as a foil to the setting itself, something not completely absent in 1st edition, by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:07:12-07:00","id":1487279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487278#post1487278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several reasons why suicide is a heavy topic, and usually conversations about vampires and suicide aren't very constructive in the middle of arguments if &quot;they would&quot; or, worse, &quot;they should&quot;.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the bottom line to it is that it isn't a normal action in any sense. It isn't strength and it isn't weakness, it isn't courage, it isn't cowardice. It is too easy, both for those who are sick and think about it and for those who don't, to imagine or say shit about it. The reality of it is messy, painful and desperate in a level most people cannot grasp even when in its actual grasp.<br /> <br /> Vampires possibly commit suicide. If you feel confident to deal with this topic with your group, go for it. If you're not sure, or worse, if you have a personal <i>opinion</i> on it and wants to <i>show your headcanon on suicide</i> to people you're not sure about... <b><u>JUST DON'T</u></b>. And it isn't necessarily a big cause of deaths among them, either, no matter how bleak you think their existence is.<br /> <br /> Yet, the point of the thread is that their existence isn't necessarily bleak. Because the very reasons why we think it would be may not be there to begin with. We can form deep connections to people we knew just a few years ago, and cope without a problem with losing old connections as time goes on and they become sweet memories. I've lost families, friends and pets through my life, yet I keep making friends, commemorating births and adopting puppies that I know will grow old and die.<br /> <br /> It isn't hard to think of a character that savors life and contributes to society just as anyone could being a mortal, once we takes in the proposed subversion of the premise and stop thinking this character in a Punk-Gothic context (even if still with a Punk-Gothic aesthetic). Actually, with a bit more effort we can have such a character even in the middle of a more &quot;regular&quot; chronicle, as a foil to the setting itself, something not completely absent in 1st edition, by the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very well put.<br /> <br /> Basically, the issue is this is really &quot;a cigar is just a cigar&quot; sort of topic.<br /> <br /> Vampirism and suicide is so far removed from actual real life concerns about being a danger to the public, loved ones, and being an immortal terror that flaps in the night that doing it as anything other fan a fantasy is....well, not going to work.<br /> <br /> At least in my humble opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T17:58:08-07:00","id":1487290,"title":"","content":"Dont really play vtm, but I feel that introverts are the most likely see vampirism as a boon. The big problem is that they probably dont want to let go of the mortal connections (however few) they have. Even introverts have parents and probably a few friends. This problem however, may solve itself when they see their family and friends die of old age or other natural causes. They will likely mourn for a while, but afterwards they will probably go on with their unlives. After all, no one lives forever, and I think vampire society (in whatever sect the vampire in question is affiliated with) kind of implies that even vampires will meet final death one day, they dont want to, but sooner or later they understand that everything comes to the end.<br /> <br /> Thats my headcanon anyway.<br /> <br /> Those who have gained the 5th dot in Path of Karma would most likely laugh at this. Path of Karma is a Sadhana unique path that allows you to choose your reincarnation beforehand, so in the event you do meet final death, you just come back as someone new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 07-20-2022, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:06:03-07:00","id":1487291,"title":"","content":"Getting bored with life is an option, but not the only one. <br /> The world is so full of places, people and experiences that some people wouldn't get bored at all even if they lived for a long time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T18:33:20-07:00","id":1487295,"title":"","content":"<b>How many murders are you allowed before its too many?</b><br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I think vampirism should be thought of as, &quot;Aside from that, Mrs. Lincoln, how was the play?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampirism should be something that is normally incredibly good and you would be extremely happy right up until you run into things that are life-alteringly horrifying. The Beast and the Hunger are things that are intertwined and increase your chance of being a murderer (accidentally or otherwise) 10,000%.<br /> <br /> I mean, how many times would you accidentally kill someone you feed on or attack them and break their necks during a frenzy before you've decided being a vampire was a bad deal?<br /> <br /> Assuming you are, for the most part, a normally empathic and feeling person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T20:35:47-07:00","id":1487309,"title":"","content":"&quot;...And together through ages of the world we have fought the long defeat.&quot;<br /> J.R.R. Tolkien, the Lord of the Rings.<br /> <br /> This is, in my humble opinion, the phrase that best describes Tolkien's work. Ultimately, it all comes to dust; even Middle Earth will one day be over, and this concept that can only be called as <i>Entropy</i> is present in the entire Tolkien's legendarium, with each passing age being less magical, less fantastic than the previous one - the first age is the age of the great evil of Morgoth, but also the great heroism of humans and elves and dwarves, and the great beauty of the Silmarills. The second age is a bit lesser version of the first, with the great powers of Morgoth gone and so too the wonder of the Silmarills, but marks the ascension of the grand kingdom of Numenor, the ascension of Sauron as new Dark Lord and the rings of power. The third age is a lesser version of the second one, with Sauron weaker and jewel that was Numenor destroyed, and Valinor forever out of the world. But, it marks the creation of Gondor and Arnor and the coming of the Istari (the five mages, among which were Saruman, Gandalf and Radagast). And finally, by the forth age, the elves are gone, there are no more dark lords, and gone too is all the wonders of the world. And Middle Earth goes, slowly, diminishing itself.<br /> <br /> And despite that, you fight; you keep fighting the long, inevitable defeat. No matter what, it will all come to an end. And yet, this is a noble fight, exactly because it's impossible. It's a call to fight for good not because it's an achievable goal, but rather because it is the right thing to do.<br /> <br /> I did play once a 4th gen methuselah that reached Golconda. My vampire characters are ALWAYS hopeful and inherently good - I at least try to make them that way. Not because of humanity or any such. And no, not because I think that the vampiric condition (in my view) is pleasurable or desirable. No, on the contrary, I always find it abominable. But rather because I always choose to fight the &quot;long defeat&quot;. No, my character will not achieve victory, or peace. Yes, he will lose in the end, either suffering a horrible death or losing himself to the beast. And yet, my characters will ALWAYS cling to hope - even thou it's a fools hope. Because the &quot;long defeat&quot; is a battle that is worth fighting, even thou the defeat is inevitable.<br /> <br /> So, althought I see VTM as a very dark game, my games paradoxically have this shine of light that never fades, no matter what.<br /> <br /> So, althought in my opinion the vampires from VTM have nothing going for them except their inevitable doom, hope and good are always present, even in the darkest places.<br /> <br /> I mean, I played I freaking 4th gen Setite, son of the dark &quot;god&quot; himself, that rejected him in his face and went on to search for Golconda for freaking sake! - and that character basically became a monk, just imagine that, one of the most powerful vampires in the world and a powerful setite sorcerour, living as a beggar in the middle of the woods, drinking blood from animals alone and self declared &quot;not in the Jihad&quot; - which I literally was; and I could ALWAYS manage to enter ANY domains unmolested, because I always had some valuable wisdom for others with which I could &quot;buy my way in&quot;. That character became a vampiric legend, sometimes refered as highly as Saulot himself, so yes, I do play VtM in a positive way. But I still think that cainites are beyond salvation - they are utterly doomed.<br /> <br /> But, exactly because they are doomed is that their fight is so much more noble, at least when they try to do the right thing despite that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T01:54:59-07:00","id":1487336,"title":"","content":"I should probably clarify from the comments I'm seeing that I'm commenting on the player trend of playing characters which are okay or even happy as vampires rather than if the setting supports it.<br /> <br /> In regards to suicidal Impulses it's a tricky subject sensitive subject matter aside. My current pc made some attempts after her first frenzy had severe ramifications but unfamiliarity gave her enough time to reconsider (partly inspired by curiosity over her increased resistance). I don't think the vampiric condition is intrinsically horrible enough to kill self genrally, while kindred are genrally unhappy in setting that's obviously a big gap before suicide","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-21-2022, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T02:25:21-07:00","id":1487341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487179#post1487179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I think about the things that give a human's life fulfillment. Meaningful long term relationships and a long term purpose that spans both day to day as well as over many years.<br /> <br /> Vampires are largely cut off from the former by virtue of their immorality, and many of the purposes humans derive fulfillment from are cut off from them via the Masquerade and inability to procreate.<br /> <br /> While I think it's entirely possible to experience a joyful, fulfilling existence as a Vampire, I think it's something the vampire must consciously choose every night.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons Masquerade is to be kept in perfect condition is to provide Vampires a place to socialize and to create long-term goals for themselves. Clan Culture helps a lot with this as well.<br /> <br /> As for procreation - not only there is the wonderful possibility of creating a Childe or adopting one, but there is also the opportunity to make a mortal a Ghoul or take care and responsbility for a group of mortals, or a particular interesting mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T16:42:15-07:00","id":1487426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487295#post1487295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How many murders are you allowed before its too many?</b><br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I think vampirism should be thought of as, &quot;Aside from that, Mrs. Lincoln, how was the play?&quot;<br /> <br /> Vampirism should be something that is normally incredibly good and you would be extremely happy right up until you run into things that are life-alteringly horrifying. The Beast and the Hunger are things that are intertwined and increase your chance of being a murderer (accidentally or otherwise) 10,000%.<br /> <br /> I mean, how many times would you accidentally kill someone you feed on or attack them and break their necks during a frenzy before you've decided being a vampire was a bad deal?<br /> <br /> Assuming you are, for the most part, a normally empathic and feeling person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Playing devils advocate for a moment, while I see what you are getting at, it feels like it is missing a core truth about existence outside of a contrived society. Namely that death is part of life and that either killing to feed or killing to keep from being eaten is natural. It is a very first world morality centric view to presume that such a natural law doesn't exist anymore or has somehow been left behind, or potentially even more dangerous, the idea that we have evolved beyond it. <br /> <br /> There are three responses to this existential truth:<br /> 1. Denial - Basically hear no evil, see no evil, speak no evil. Label anything that makes one uncomfortable as evil. Ignore the possibility of this reality affecting you and then freak out or break down when life hits you with it.<br /> <br /> 2. Obsession - This one truth becomes the only truth. Blood for the Blood God! Milk for the Khorne-flakes, etc. Every desire and bad behavior is validated by concepts like &quot;The strong eat, the weak are meat&quot;, &quot;Survival of the Fittest&quot;, and the classic &quot;kill before being killed&quot;. Rather than being aware, the focus is laughing at the collateral damage.<br /> <br /> 3. Acceptance - There will always be violence, strife, winners and losers, the eater and the eaten. The only thing you can do is be ready to fight when required, capable of running when prudent, and always considering what any given course of action or inaction gets you as a result. Can you kill a threat to you or your interests, sure. But at the same time you are aware of the diminishing returns on carving a bloody swath through all who stand in your way.<br /> <br /> VtM tries very hard to force the discussion to only be about Denial or Obsession, but then tries to sweep Acceptance under the rug like an uninvited party guest. This is born out by how the various morality paths are handled and how Golconda is not exactly mechanically functional.<br /> <br /> I mean I have never heard of games where people ran an entire coterie who were all post Golconda. I have heard many variations of &quot;played a tzimisce who skinned a baby with a cheese grater and used its still living body as a fleshlight&quot;, but practically no games where the vampires are at peace with what they are. Admittedly the instant you focus on acceptance, that can fall into a &quot;Vampions&quot; style setup very easily. But if the antics of the superheroes in &quot;The Boys&quot; are anything to go by, then Vampires can easily be &quot;heroes&quot; without losing that dark edge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T17:11:28-07:00","id":1487427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487426#post1487426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Playing devils advocate for a moment, while I see what you are getting at, it feels like it is missing a core truth about existence outside of a contrived society. Namely that death is part of life and that either killing to feed or killing to keep from being eaten is natural. It is a very first world morality centric view to presume that such a natural law doesn't exist anymore or has somehow been left behind, or potentially even more dangerous, the idea that we have evolved beyond it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which gets to a core truth about Vampire: The Masquerade really.<br /> <br /> 1. Are vampires natural? There's a very good argument that vampires are not in any way natural but the embodiment of unnatural. Or is the denial that tortures you? Those who try to live like lions or bears as predators may be on to something or they may simply be taking a nose dive into the Beast because vampires are a supernatural curse that divorces you from the world as it should be.<br /> <br /> 2. Does &quot;natural&quot; matter in the slightest? <i>Shatterpoint</i> by Matthew Stover, oddly, was a pretty good adaptation of Nieztsche to the Jedi of all people. Basically highlighting that &quot;civilization&quot; is about smacking down the natural and that good is a wholly unnatural construct. However, that's what makes it right.<br /> <br /> The best conversations about V:TM that I've had about morality weren't &quot;weepy vampire feels bad about himself&quot; but discussing the fact that you are a being that is probably going to be a plague on the rest of mankind and a negative net-bad no matter what you do. HOWEVER, that doesn't mean you don't want to live or that you're obligated to destroy yourself or other vampires. It just means you learn to live with the fact you're the bad guy and maybe do as little evil as you can along the way.<br /> <br /> I think these are some of the best roleplaying opportunities for gamers.<br /> <br /> Like, &quot;Yes, I'm doing the selfish and wrong thing but that doesn't mean I have to be as evil as possible either.&quot;<br /> <br /> And you can have the alternative answers:<br /> <br /> * If you can't be &quot;good&quot; then be a different kind of monsters and seek a Path or Road.<br /> <br /> * Maybe being an animal can still teach you to be better.<br /> <br /> * Maybe you are evil but maybe you can still be a net good by being an enemy to worse people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-21-2022, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T18:59:19-07:00","id":1487433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487427#post1487427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Are vampires natural? There's a very good argument that vampires are not in any way natural but the embodiment of unnatural. Or is the denial that tortures you? Those who try to live like lions or bears as predators may be on to something or they may simply be taking a nose dive into the Beast because vampires are a supernatural curse that divorces you from the world as it should be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would vote that vampires are natural, namely because they are made from natural humans. All of their emotional issues, their psychological problems, their drives, are just adjusted or amped up versions of human ones. Sure the backstory of a divine curse and such places it in the supernatural category, but in the setting of WoD that is a natural part of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487427#post1487427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Does &quot;natural&quot; matter in the slightest? <i>Shatterpoint</i> by Matthew Stover, oddly, was a pretty good adaptation of Nieztsche to the Jedi of all people. Basically highlighting that &quot;civilization&quot; is about smacking down the natural and that good is a wholly unnatural construct. However, that's what makes it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that civilization is about creating an artificial space with an environment and group related rules that is controlled by the creators of said space. As for if it was natural or not, I think creatures like Ants, Termites, and naked mole rats would tend push it into the natural category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487427#post1487427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best conversations about V:TM that I've had about morality weren't &quot;weepy vampire feels bad about himself&quot; but discussing the fact that you are a being that is probably going to be a plague on the rest of mankind and a negative net-bad no matter what you do. HOWEVER, that doesn't mean you don't want to live or that you're obligated to destroy yourself or other vampires. It just means you learn to live with the fact you're the bad guy and maybe do as little evil as you can along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps I am showing my age, but to me that is just a question of being immature verses growing up. VtM as a system doesn't support the exploration of a &quot;mature&quot; mentality regardless of the monstrousness of the existence. By mature, I don't mean adult themes, I mean an experienced, stoic, and measured approach to existence.<br /> <br /> The Gentleman Gamer had a youtube video a long time ago that mentioned how Americans were great at portraying tortured souls, but rarely played glorious monsters of grace and poise. While you can role play any way you want, the mechanics and fluff are very stilted towards emo teenager or mental health patient, rather than a predatory and refined existence.<br /> <br /> Then again, I could just be really weird for valuing the game space that is normally reserved for character retirement or post end game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T19:42:35-07:00","id":1487436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487433#post1487433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I am showing my age, but to me that is just a question of being immature verses growing up. VtM as a system doesn't support the exploration of a &quot;mature&quot; mentality regardless of the monstrousness of the existence. By mature, I don't mean adult themes, I mean an experienced, stoic, and measured approach to existence.<br /> <br /> The Gentleman Gamer had a youtube video a long time ago that mentioned how Americans were great at portraying tortured souls, but rarely played glorious monsters of grace and poise. While you can role play any way you want, the mechanics and fluff are very stilted towards emo teenager or mental health patient, rather than a predatory and refined existence.<br /> <br /> Then again, I could just be really weird for valuing the game space that is normally reserved for character retirement or post end game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that it's actually just taking the punk mentality and maintaining that as the gameline's ethos.<br /> <br /> <b>Punk view on &quot;selling out&quot;</b>: There's nothing mature about surrendering to being a predatory parasite on the human existence. The Elders given given up and they're scumbags for it. Because it will eventually be either you or them. They should be treated as figures of contempt rather than celebrated as making an informed and mature choice.<br /> <br /> <b>Non-Punk view on Elder</b>: If it is actually impossible to stay the straight and narrow path, to do the &quot;right&quot; thing when biologically and societally there are no options but &quot;die a hero or live long to become the villain&quot; then it is just silly to resist.<br /> <br /> But whether this is a mature choice is something that line itself has danced back and forth on.<br /> <br /> Oddly, there is a biological third option. Thin Bloods can live on animal blood, do not frenzy, and will live forever. They are the heralds of a morally acceptable and sustainable vampire existence.<br /> <br /> It's the older vampire generations that are incapable of living peacefully with humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T21:32:19-07:00","id":1487446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487436#post1487436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that it's actually just taking the punk mentality and maintaining that as the gameline's ethos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel that punk is the flavor of the month, while vampire is the core flavor. Otherwise things like the Dark Ages setting, Victorian age setting, etc. wouldn't work without the &quot;Punk&quot;. Once again this is a question of modern morality and values being seen as primary rather than just the current fad. When an individuals perspective is measured by centuries or millennia, contemporary ideals lose a lot of weight.<br /> <br /> As for why hold onto standards and self discipline if the slide is inevitable? The answer is because self discipline also gives you power. Those that can not attain or maintain self discipline end up using the argument that it is a useless fight because they have given up.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Die a hero or live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot; only holds up if you stop the timeline once you hit villain status. It becomes cyclical, from revolutionary hero, to the protector of the establishment, to epitome of everything wrong with society, back to revolutionary hero once you revolt against whatever is currently the state of things. Figure on several decades or centuries between each title shift, but with enough time it all rotates around.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means that morality as a whole can be akin to waiting for bell bottom pants or certain hair styles to come back into style, but from an Immortals perspective, that is how it works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487436#post1487436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oddly, there is a biological third option. Thin Bloods can live on animal blood, do not frenzy, and will live forever. They are the heralds of a morally acceptable and sustainable vampire existence.<br /> <br /> It's the older vampire generations that are incapable of living peacefully with humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this amusing because the Thinbloods generally can't win against their more potent kin due to mechanical restrictions, and those that do win tend to lower their Generation as a means of survival.<br /> <br /> Also living peacefully with humans is not the same as not feeding on humans. Any young vampire can live off animal blood and butcher humans for fun. Any Elder can feed off human blood and never kill to feed.<br /> <br /> Seriously, in a society where we have Sugar Babies and Only Fans, can you argue that it would all that difficult to ethically hire a Herd? It only becomes an ethical problem if you default to the tropes of Dom/Sub abuse, use of supernatural coercion, or just good old fashion kidnapping. You could even tap your mortal family for blood. I mean how many people would be willing to donate a blood bag per month to a Great Grand Parent if it means assistance in paying off their student loan debts?<br /> <br /> Admittedly I am a fan of the Kindred of the East setting where the concept of the supernatural and mundane coexisting is an established theme. So, to me there is more wiggle room for non-destructive vampirism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T21:46:30-07:00","id":1487447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487446#post1487446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also living peacefully with humans is not the same as not feeding on humans. Any young vampire can live off animal blood and butcher humans for fun. Any Elder can feed off human blood and never kill to feed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit, if I had to add any V5 elements to V20 and earlier editions, these are the only unquestionably good ideas. Codeifying the lack of feeding restrictions to Higher Generations.<br /> <br /> It gives a reason to play 10th, 11th, and 13th generations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-21T21:56:23-07:00","id":1487448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487446#post1487446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel that punk is the flavor of the month, while vampire is the core flavor. Otherwise things like the Dark Ages setting, Victorian age setting, etc. wouldn't work without the &quot;Punk&quot;. Once again this is a question of modern morality and values being seen as primary rather than just the current fad. When an individuals perspective is measured by centuries or millennia, contemporary ideals lose a lot of weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> I guess if the vampires would come out (sorry, lack of better words) they would be either treated as the Mutants of X-Men... or it simply would work. I mean even not the World of Darkness, wich is darker and more horrible place than ours, our world is pretty harsh place and there is a good fundation for it<br /> The whole started with Stroker's Dracula, and Vlad's little &quot;masquarade breach attempt&quot; how they call it was actually the best thing that happened with the vampires in the past thosuands of years<br /> They became celebrities, tragic heroes, everyone wanted a dark mysterious stranger who seduces him, vampires became something People actually wanted to be real!<br /> Arguably this phenomenon still exist <br /> Sure it would cause some fear and trouble, but the benefits outweight the dangers. For example, Historians would cream in their pants just thinking the possibility of talking someone who was actually there and seen what happened, or was part of it,<br /> Maybe would work, maybe not<br /> Probably not, since WoD is WoD<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487446#post1487446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly I am a fan of the Kindred of the East setting where the concept of the supernatural and mundane coexisting is an established theme. So, to me there is more wiggle room for non-destructive vampirism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey! I'm not alone! Neat!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T08:16:45-07:00","id":1487481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487448#post1487448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey! I'm not alone! Neat!</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely not. While the Orientalism of it is objectively bad, KotE and the other &quot;East&quot; lines are extremely popular because of their take in the setting in general. Take out the Exotic Asia tone and it is actually an extremely solid setting, in many aspects more than the usual.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I completely agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar727_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"727\" data-vbnamecard=\"727\">Thoth</a> on this. The setting makes a lot of assumptions, it assumes a modern Christian ethos, a Punk view of the world, a Gothic mood for the character. None of those are necessary. As I said elsewhere, we are just as predatory and parasitic on the real world as vampires, yet it never stopped us from being ethical and/or moral (not the same thing). Neither in the many other ways there is to be such, nor in the current fashion.<br /> <br /> And people with blood addiction exist, they're not monsters because of that. Vampirism is a metaphor on abuse and rape, but that doesn't mean this is innate to their condition, it is only a fucking trope!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T21:50:46-07:00","id":1487541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487446#post1487446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that punk is the flavor of the month, while vampire is the core flavor. Otherwise things like the Dark Ages setting, Victorian age setting, etc. wouldn't work without the &quot;Punk&quot;. Once again this is a question of modern morality and values being seen as primary rather than just the current fad. When an individuals perspective is measured by centuries or millennia, contemporary ideals lose a lot of weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to give a disagreement there but that's because punk is a sensibility that works surprisingly well with the presentation of not only the other settings you've listed but also history as a whole. Punk is primarily a rejection of social norms and establishment of a nihilistic skepticism of romanticism toward inequity and traditional morality that were being forward during the Eighties.<br /> <br /> A &quot;punk&quot; interpretation of the Dark Ages is almost inevitable with any sense of realism because the majority of modern gamers are not going to be people who believe in the divine right of kings, will be skeptical of the absolute authority of the church, and will certainly reject a great deal of the ethnocentrism of Europe in the 12th century. The simple rejection of these facts puts V:TDA as a work that strongly questions the underpinnings of said society and vampires as people who can live outside the stratified social hierarchy.<br /> <br /> A &quot;punk&quot; interpretation of the Victorian Era is the ONLY way I could ever play it because the sheer racism of the British Empire and horror of colonialism (and not just in &quot;far off&quot; countries but right next door in Ireland) plus the inequities of the Industrial Revolution mean that I'd assume you'd be missing most of the better part of the roleplaying opportunities if you're all upper crust white men. There's a reason Alan Moore wrote the League of Extraordinary Gentleman and it's taking a massive piss on the values of the 19th Century.<br /> <br /> Baked into the heart of V:TM with its vampirism is the realization that punk values and vampire values (for lack of a better term) are fundamentally the same. Which is to say that Goth and Punk are not so far removed. Anne Rice's Interview with a Vampire and many other influential vampire works like Poppy Z Bright and The Lost Boys have vampires representing beings who live outside traditional moral structures.<br /> <br /> Which makes your objection kind of ironic because you see punk as one of these structures while I see it as the shattering of convention.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I think you raise some very good points but I think we just disagree on the punk sensibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for why hold onto standards and self discipline if the slide is inevitable? The answer is because self discipline also gives you power. Those that can not attain or maintain self discipline end up using the argument that it is a useless fight because they have given up.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Die a hero or live long enough to see yourself become the villain&quot; only holds up if you stop the timeline once you hit villain status. It becomes cyclical, from revolutionary hero, to the protector of the establishment, to epitome of everything wrong with society, back to revolutionary hero once you revolt against whatever is currently the state of things. Figure on several decades or centuries between each title shift, but with enough time it all rotates around.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means that morality as a whole can be akin to waiting for bell bottom pants or certain hair styles to come back into style, but from an Immortals perspective, that is how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good rebuttal and I acknowledge it.<br /> <br /> Still, I think it depends on how much we believe vampires yo-yo versus slide to doom. How many vampires ever actually crawl out of the degeneration of their Humanity/Roads? A very good number of them may actually just end up becoming monsters that are killed by their younger members who want their power/are disgusted by their actions or fellows who maintain scruples. How many survive to being wights? We may never know but that number could be pretty high by itself.<br /> <br /> Even when wightdom was not &quot;slavering animal-like monster&quot;, the implications of 1st Edition was when you hit Humanity 0 there was no redemption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this amusing because the Thinbloods generally can't win against their more potent kin due to mechanical restrictions, and those that do win tend to lower their Generation as a means of survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a trap, though, as you might argue it's much better to be a Thin Blood and take advantage of your human like qualities versus trying to beat the Elders at their own game.<br /> <br /> But yes, very good thoughts here on your part.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T23:31:17-07:00","id":1487551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487541#post1487541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A &quot;punk&quot; interpretation of the Dark Ages is almost inevitable with any sense of realism because the majority of modern gamers</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's exactly his point, actually, that you're missing.<br /> <br /> A Punk approach is easy to apply to a historical game because <b><i>the players</i></b> are modern people with modern sensibilities. But <b><i>the characters</i></b> are not. A character with a Punk ethos is actually an anachronism. Criticism to the social rules of the time did existed, but it had completely distinct context, connotation, values.<br /> <br /> So that's still the same problem: the setting is predicated upon a set of values and view of reality that aren't as intrinsic to the human condition as the setting itself claims to be the case. <b>DAV</b> and <b>Victorian Age</b> are Punk because they claim those modern values to be objective natural reality and, as such, the values under which such characters should live and/or be judged by the players.<br /> <br /> To be honest I would go even further, because I think that even giving those values a broad &quot;modern&quot; stamp may be a problem if you end up thinking those values are <b><u>the</u></b> modern values. They are a set of values that are modern, a modern take on a particular mindset common in some current populations. But even in modern times it is hard to objectively state the values predicated by the game as a universal phenomena or even as the standard conclusion of Ethics, Philosophy or anything else. Actually they're very crude outside the confines of genre.<br /> <br /> More importantly here, for a work of fiction predicated upon this Punk-Gothic mix of genre and tropes, the standard values and mood of the game are perfectly valid, no problem. <b>But under the proposal of analyzing a premise subversion</b> it is utterly foolish to be attached to them except in the sense of maybe saying you wouldn't be personally able to go with this subversion. The whole point is that many players run characters that simply and truthfully enjoy being vampires, and whether those characters are moral or not under any particular set of values, the fact remains that those characters <b>themselves</b> are not predicated upon the setting's values.<br /> <br /> No one is evaluating the values and ethos of the game and if they work within the premise. That's not the point. The point is to subvert the very premise, and as such the values and ethos upon which it is predicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T23:48:53-07:00","id":1487552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487551#post1487551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's exactly his point, actually, that you're missing.<br /> <br /> A Punk approach is easy to apply to a historical game because <b><i>the players</i></b> are modern people with modern sensibilities. But <b><i>the characters</i></b> are not. A character with a Punk ethos is actually an anachronism. Criticism to the social rules of the time did existed, but it had completely distinct context, connotation, values.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me actually turn that around on you. It's not that I don't agree but that I actually see it as a virtue and inherent part of the vampire existence in The Dark Ages and why it makes it easier to do the game as a modern person.<br /> <br /> A vampire in the Dark Ages is going to inherently be a punk.<br /> <br /> (exaggerating a bit for hyperbole)<br /> <br /> The Embrace shatters you from the status of nobility, serfdom, peasantry, or priestly vocation. You are given powers that inherently disrupt the social order and are either damned by said social order or forced to seek an alternative heretical interpretation of it. Part of why vampirism and punk goes together so well is Middle Ages or Victorian Era or Modern, you are <i>free</i> of your previous life.<br /> <br /> And most likely encouraged by your newfound status to tear back at the society that you are from.<br /> <br /> Or rule it.<br /> <br /> Either way.<br /> <br /> Lestat was born in 1760 but he's still a man who absolutely rebels against all level of social conformity save, possibly, the fact that other people are lesser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T05:22:36-07:00","id":1487567,"title":"","content":"Edit-Pointless tangent","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 07-23-2022, 08:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T05:50:21-07:00","id":1487571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487552#post1487552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Embrace shatters you from the status of nobility, serfdom, peasantry, or priestly vocation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about the merchant class and the tradesmen (not the serfs, I mean the various craftsmen in the cities) ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487552#post1487552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are given powers that inherently disrupt the social order and are either damned by said social order or forced to seek an alternative heretical interpretation of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't this directly imply that most persons in the Middle Ages were true and honest followers of various beliefs and social orders? The way I see it most were sort of indifferent and selfish in this regard. Most notably the priesthood and the nobility <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T06:24:55-07:00","id":1487580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487433#post1487433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would vote that vampires are natural, namely because they are made from natural humans. All of their emotional issues, their psychological problems, their drives, are just adjusted or amped up versions of human ones. Sure the backstory of a divine curse and such places it in the supernatural category, but in the setting of WoD that is a natural part of the setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I would say that civilization is about creating an artificial space with an environment and group related rules that is controlled by the creators of said space. As for if it was natural or not, I think creatures like Ants, Termites, and naked mole rats would tend push it into the natural category.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Perhaps I am showing my age, but to me that is just a question of being immature verses growing up. VtM as a system doesn't support the exploration of a &amp;quot;mature&amp;quot; mentality regardless of the monstrousness of the existence. By mature, I don't mean adult themes, I mean an experienced, stoic, and measured approach to existence.<br /> <br /> The Gentleman Gamer had a youtube video a long time ago that mentioned how Americans were great at portraying tortured souls, but rarely played glorious monsters of grace and poise. While you can role play any way you want, the mechanics and fluff are very stilted towards emo teenager or mental health patient, rather than a predatory and refined existence.<br /> <br /> Then again, I could just be really weird for valuing the game space that is normally reserved for character retirement or post end game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing wrong with playing an emo teenager.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T06:49:53-07:00","id":1487583,"title":"","content":"the group that i'm running are all thinbloods who spent a good chunk of the campaign being all THIS IS AWESOME, LET'S DO SOME HEISTS until the hopelessness of their situation began to really creep in and i think that really accentuated the horror aspect of the game.<br /> (also! the only game of 'vampire' i played, ages ago, was with people who just treated the condition as a supervillain origin and it was one of the worst games, of any kind, that i've ever played and i bailed after the third night.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T06:57:42-07:00","id":1487585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487580#post1487580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing wrong with playing an emo teenager.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, an emo teenager is a good starting place for a character. But I also feel that given the harshness of the setting, they must eventually change, grow stronger, become more cunning, more self disciplined, etc. to survive.<br /> <br /> The Kindred of the East books had a term for this exact sort of fledgling, a &quot;running monkey&quot; which covered the first century of unlife for a new vampire. They were expected to revel in their new power, tend to left over business from their mortal days, and more or less be non-stop collateral damage. But after that point they were expected to act like a proper monster, rather than a spring breaker with fangs. This is why I tend to frown whenever I see a vampire write up which makes them centuries old, never gone into torpor, and yet are still acting like a highschooler.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, I could be just old enough that I should start looking to invest in a rocking chair for the front porch so I can properly holler at the whippersnappers to get off my lawn. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T07:08:20-07:00","id":1487586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487447#post1487447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, if I had to add any V5 elements to V20 and earlier editions, these are the only unquestionably good ideas. Codeifying the lack of feeding restrictions to Higher Generations.<br /> <br /> It gives a reason to play 10th, 11th, and 13th generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Random side idea, how would you feel about the ability to Ghoul or create a new vampire were &quot;disciplines&quot; rather than automatic vampire powers? I ask because more than feeding restrictions, I see the lack of an inherent population control restriction as one of the more setting breaking aspects.<br /> <br /> Yes, a Prince can claim the right to allow for creating new vampires in their territory, but they can't exactly complain if you leave their area of control, sire a childe, then return after a few years.<br /> <br /> But by the mechanics, the mass embracing/ghouling of towns, cities, military bases, etc. are all viable strategies. Conversely a shifter or mage group has to hope a new member is born eventually and then wait 15 to 20 years for them to mature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T07:50:38-07:00","id":1487588,"title":"","content":"Using 1/4th rather than 3/4ths of the day is horrendous, and drinking blood to live is going to be difficult at first, but these are things you get used to. The main concern is the political horror, but even that's mitigatable: If you go by pre-5, the Beast is something you can deal with, if you go by V5, you'll probably experience the power of agentic shift in regards to the Beast. It's fine. The real issues are political, but even then you can mitigate them pretty well and live for hundreds of years. <br /> <br /> My early characters were always ambitious and paranoid. In-game Paranoia gets you to do some crazy shit. This would spill over into a bit of out of game paranoia (IE The ST will screw me over if I don't detail or justify everything) also helps. Later on, I realised I was doing things wrong: you're not up against the world, you're part of the conspiracy along with every other vampire: don't lose yourself to short term ambition, be everyone's supportive best friend, don't be afraid of a little debt, don't worry about resources, don't worry too much about the other players, The tighter you grasp, the more everything slips away. Just accept your relative lack of control. Also, OoC, I think that if the ST knows you're careful and paranoid, he's more likely to have fun screwing with you than the less careful characters. <br /> <br /> Rather than take 5 dots of Generation like a noob, it's far better for your character's mental health to take a good social starting point. This will lead to better decisions. Just like RL, A good relationship with your parental figure is the best thing for the development of a neonate: <b>Mentor is one of the best backgrounds for staying sane</b>. It's help when you need it, shelter when you need it, and it's deterrence. Unless you're planning to be an interdependent coterie, it's essential for neonates. 1 mostly just wards off small fries, 2+ is enough to keep most happy with you. Status kinda works in it's place if you don't want Mentor (I haven't seen it really used so much). The second thing on the list is Domain. If you've got at least two dots to yourself, you've got a great foundation to accumulate other backgrounds; you don't need to have your businesses or herd in your domain, but it sure makes things easier. After you've got these two things (and perhaps pool domain with your mentor) what comes next is up to you. <br /> <br /> <b>If the sire (and by extension, the player) plans his neonate's starting point smartly and properly educates a half-decent choice of childer, that childe will have few serious difficulties and will become a valued and productive member of the sire's brood and the wider cityscape and sect</b>. If we're very filial, the childe can even run the sire's things while he's in Torpor. A wholesome, long lasting partnership of mutual benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:39:01-07:00","id":1487607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487583#post1487583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the group that i'm running are all thinbloods who spent a good chunk of the campaign being all THIS IS AWESOME, LET'S DO SOME HEISTS until the hopelessness of their situation began to really creep in and i think that really accentuated the horror aspect of the game.<br /> (also! the only game of 'vampire' i played, ages ago, was with people who just treated the condition as a supervillain origin and it was one of the worst games, of any kind, that i've ever played and i bailed after the third night.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampires from Anne Rice pretty much lean towards this idea of acceptance. Lestat, Marius, Armand. They dont treat mortals as unworth of note or as playthings for their unending pleasure, but simply accept their condition as top predators who ocasionally will kill. Even Lois end up accepting this fact, althought it's a much harder struggle initially.<br /> <br /> Despite that however, they are all and each one of them... Hollow. Eventually, immortality takes its toll, even for the most enthusiastic of them. They end up empty inside, and seeking some company to fill the void - at least for a while.<br /> <br /> And Akasha is just completely inhuman in every way, so she's more like the third option of &quot;sacrifices to the blood Gods!&quot; rather than just acceptance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T09:49:07-07:00","id":1487610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487586#post1487586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Random side idea, how would you feel about the ability to Ghoul or create a new vampire were &amp;quot;disciplines&amp;quot; rather than automatic vampire powers? I ask because more than feeding restrictions, I see the lack of an inherent population control restriction as one of the more setting breaking aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Im sorry, I didnt exactly understand, could you elaborate? What do you mean exactly, like a sort of &quot;power&quot; to create a new vampire?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487586#post1487586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a Prince can claim the right to allow for creating new vampires in their territory, but they can't exactly complain if you leave their area of control, sire a childe, then return after a few years.<br /> <br /> But by the mechanics, the mass embracing/ghouling of towns, cities, military bases, etc. are all viable strategies. Conversely a shifter or mage group has to hope a new member is born eventually and then wait 15 to 20 years for them to mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, if you leave a city for a few years, there's nothing that says that the Prince has to take you back in. Since you left your domain vacant, you no longer owns it, and upon return you would have to request permission to remain back again.<br /> <br /> Also, even if the Prince/Primogen allows you to stay again, that doesnt automatically translate into permission for your child too. The Prince/Primogen could allow you but refuse your child, or even refusing both. And that would be a problem for the both of you.<br /> <br /> And, given your clear rebellious nature, you would probably be VERY unwelcomed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T10:19:33-07:00","id":1487616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487552#post1487552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me actually turn that around on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't. You kept not understanding the point.<br /> <br /> It being a virtue or not is completely irrelevant. The proposal of the thread is to examine doing something else.<br /> <br /> And defining any rebellion against conformity as Punk is an extremely broad and pointless definition of Punk just for the sake of using the same word instead of making any meaningful examination of the characteristics of the actual Punk Movement in contrast to other counter-cultural movements across History.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487610#post1487610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Im sorry, I didnt exactly understand, could you elaborate? What do you mean exactly, like a sort of &quot;power&quot; to create a new vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>He means exploring how the setting would change if instead of Embrace and Ghouling being innate and almost free abilities for every vampire, they were naturally scarce, making population growth the hard part instead of growth mitigation.<br /> <br /> Requiem already has a greater restriction in that it demands Willpower expenditure along with the blood, and for the Embrace it is a permanent dot. So while everyone can do it, the Embrace is far more invested as a process (it compensates, though, with Revenants as something no vampire can completely avoid, even just an eventual victim of feeding runs a risk of coming up as a Revenant years later upon dying of other causes).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T11:08:14-07:00","id":1487623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487616#post1487616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He means exploring how the setting would change if instead of Embrace and Ghouling being innate and almost free abilities for every vampire, they were naturally scarce, making population growth the hard part instead of growth mitigation.<br /> <br /> Requiem already has a greater restriction in that it demands Willpower expenditure along with the blood, and for the Embrace it is a permanent dot. So while everyone can do it, the Embrace is far more invested as a process (it compensates, though, with Revenants as something no vampire can completely avoid, even just an eventual victim of feeding runs a risk of coming up as a Revenant years later upon dying of other causes).</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Well, like I always claim pretty much everywhere, I enjoy making adaptations, and I have the players to indulge me in my lunacy luckly. Once upon a time, long ago, I was thinking about doing something in that line, which also ressembles Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, my thinkering was first to divorce &quot;generation&quot; from the distance to a mythical creator, and instead use &quot;Blood Potency&quot; which would be more a measure of time - at first at least. <br /> <br /> Actually... I may just rescue that idea once again.<br /> <br /> I havent worked it out all too much, but a table more or less like this would do:<br /> <b>Blood Potency</b><br /> 1 - Fledgeling<br /> 2 - 1 year<br /> 3 - 5 years<br /> 4 - 10 years<br /> 5 - 50 years<br /> 6 - 100 years<br /> 7 - 500 years<br /> 8 - 1000 years<br /> 9 - 5000 years<br /> 10 - 10.000 years<br /> <br /> So basically, a 1 Blood Potency would be like a 13th gen, and 10 like a 3rd gen.<br /> <br /> Now, there would be some downsizes of higher potency; I was initially thinking that for each point of potency you'd need the same amount of blood per vitae restored. For example, if you have Potency 3, you need to drink 3 points of blood from a mortal in order to restore 1 vitae to your pool.<br /> <br /> That would go up to 5 Potency. After that, you'd need vampiric Blood only; so, Potency 6 means 1 Vitae from a Potency 1 vampire to restore 1 vitae of your pool, Potency 7 needs 2 vitae per point restored and so on.<br /> <br /> Also, drinking from vamps with higher Potency is better - each Potency 2 vamps vitae is like 2 vitae from a Potency 1, Potency 3 is 3 times as nourishing and so on.<br /> <br /> And at Potency 10, only diablerri can quenchy your thristy.<br /> <br /> So, there would be some advantages to reducing your Potency, with Potency 5 being the rule for older vampires that still live in the vampiric society.<br /> <br /> How do vampires reduce their Potency? The first way is by going into Torpor. Potency is reduced in the inversed time. For instance, to reduce from Potency 6 to 5, you would have to go into Torpor for 100 years.<br /> <br /> The second and easier way, is to sireing progeny.<br /> <br /> Each progeny that you sire reduces your Potency by 1. And your Progeny's Potence equals your new rating -1. Therefore, if you have Potency 6 and you Embrace, you'll go down to Potency 5 and your Progeny's Potency will already start at 4.<br /> <br /> This also means that ANY vampire needs AT LEAST Potency 3 to Embrace; if a Potency 2 Embraces someone, the vamp loses 1 Potency but the target DIES; if a Potency 1 tries, BOTH DIE.<br /> <br /> This means that no vampire can Embrace more than once every 5 years.<br /> <br /> This leads to several changes in vampiric society - including elders methusas becoming hunters hunted, and Princes FORCING all vampires to embrace AS OFTEN AS THEY CAN in order to keep cainite pops stable, and having to keep a balance between decent stable numbers and somewhat decent Potency - as I was also planning to have Potency to be added to dice pools or some such","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T11:25:24-07:00","id":1487626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487586#post1487586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a Prince can claim the right to allow for creating new vampires in their territory, but they can't exactly complain if you leave their area of control, sire a childe, then return after a few years.</div> </div> </div> </div>in such a scenario I think the prince would enquire if the current number of vampires is sustainable if it not then the prince could deport some of the neonates but of course depending on the circumstances this could be easier said then done.<br /> <br /> ideally the prince would catch on to the fact that his subjects were looking for a loophole to sire people by simply leaving the prince's city and coming back with their new childe, the prince now armed with this knowledge can do one of two things 1) allow the sire to remain but forbid the childe from entering the city on pain of death. 2) the prince can just invoke the third tradition and kill both the sire and childe because as this third law states 'thou shall only sire another with the permission of thine elder, if thou createst another without thine elder's leave both thou and thy progeny shall be slain' and the prince is the elder of the city he rules even if he not old enough to be called such so any vampire siring a human without their prince say so even if they do so outside of the city the vampire is still getting their head cut off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:49:57-07:00","id":1487667,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27369\" data-vbnamecard=\"27369\">The smiling gun-knight</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24689\" data-vbnamecard=\"24689\">Kakost</a> the way both of you are viewing the Prince is dependent on VtM being a street level game.<br /> <br /> 1. The tradition of the elder giving permission was originally supposed to be permission from your sire or higher of your own bloodline to expand the family, Princes have argued that they also have that power. But if you are in a different domain and get permission from your sire or from a different prince, then the first prince doesn't have a right to complain. Yes they can proclaim that the domain can not sustain additional vampires, but since no crime was inherently committed, the childer can only stay temporarily, just like any other kindred who is just passing through.<br /> <br /> 2. Speaking of temporary, how long is that exactly? If a vampire in the domain owns property, has mortal retainers who maintain it, and the vampire goes into Torpor for a couple decades, does the vampire lose their property just because he missed some club house meetings? If a vampire often travels, does that mean he can't have a permanent home to come back to? While during the Dark Ages it made sense that cities were islands of survival for vampires, once we hit the Victorian Age, the Old West or the Modern era, vampires aren't restricted from being mobile or getting boons from multiple Princes.<br /> <br /> 3. How does a Princes authority apply when you own property, an industry, or some other power in multiple cities? Most STs and players tend to think in single city/domain storyline terms. In reality though an individual can have &quot;domain&quot; across multiple cities and not need to be kindred. From character generation you can make an Elon Musk, Jeff Bezos, or Bill Gates type, but if you have houses/havens in multiple states, factories in multiple countries, and a thriving internet business, exactly which Prince do you have to listen to? Does the prince who rules where your house is or where your server farm have rule over you?<br /> <br /> This is why I poke at the concept that V:tM lore, traditions, and fluff is more Lost Boys biker gang vampires than vampire power brokers or CEOs. The rules and mechanics just don't connect with business realties after the age of discovery. Once you have colonies or international business groups, those notions of city states kind of fall apart.<br /> <br /> Playing an emo teen vampire drifter, professional assassin, or Lestat style rocker can be cool, but occasionally running a business CEO type can be fun as well. The rules and mechanics just tend to face plant into a brick wall when you start thinking in those terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T17:56:37-07:00","id":1487669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487623#post1487623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see. Well, like I always claim pretty much everywhere, I enjoy making adaptations, and I have the players to indulge me in my lunacy luckly. Once upon a time, long ago, I was thinking about doing something in that line, which also ressembles Requiem.<br /> <br /> So, my thinkering was first to divorce &quot;generation&quot; from the distance to a mythical creator, and instead use &quot;Blood Potency&quot; which would be more a measure of time - at first at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting take on it.<br /> <br /> I was thinking more along the lines of a Ghouling discipline which means your minions are soul bonded to you so there is a cap on how many ghouls you can maintain at any given time, like one or two per dot of the Ghouling discipline. The higher your score the less often you have to feed them blood to maintain the connection.<br /> <br /> As for the restriction on creating new vampires, I was thinking far more harsh than Requiem. More along the lines that creating a childer had the chances of something going wrong, like a partial embrace where the childer is a vampire but in a permanent coma, or if things go really wrong the childer consumes the sires soul in the turning attempt. The higher the Embracing score the less risky it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T18:00:26-07:00","id":1487670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487586#post1487586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, a Prince can claim the right to allow for creating new vampires in their territory, but they can't exactly complain if you leave their area of control, sire a childe, then return after a few years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious if this is deliberate because this is actually literally the first political move in the entire history of Vampire: The Masquerade.<br /> <br /> Chicago vampires were going to Modius' domain of Gary to Embrace their children then return to Chicago.<br /> <br /> Lodin promptly said that any child Embraced in Gary had to present themselves to him for judgement and that any vampires Embraced in Gary needed his permission.<br /> <br /> But I think I've made my opinion that all things V:TM should revolve around Chicago clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T20:08:04-07:00","id":1487678,"title":"","content":"Yeah, anybody who leaves a city, Embraces and Childe and then walks back into the city as a way to give the Prince the finger had better be prepared for the Prince to come down hard on them. And I don't think anybody would really hold that against the Prince. If you want to blatantly flout the Prince's authority like that, you'd better be prepared for consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T20:27:41-07:00","id":1487680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487678#post1487678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, anybody who leaves a city, Embraces and Childe and then walks back into the city as a way to give the Prince the finger had better be prepared for the Prince to come down hard on them. And I don't think anybody would really hold that against the Prince. If you want to blatantly flout the Prince's authority like that, you'd better be prepared for consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if you try that bullshit, you better be expected to have plans to stay away for at least a decade or so. Which most vampires won't be willing to risk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:37:27-07:00","id":1487695,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine that for the most part, traveling to other cities is something vampires have to do with other vampires vouching for them (They need to get letters of good standing, to be followed up by a call to another city to ) and/or the traveler bringing with them significant gifts so that they may gain access to the territories of others to feed. <br /> <br /> Without permission to embrace, Disappearing and bringing back a childe who hasn't gotten any recognition in other cities is the same as never having left to embrace. You're in trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-23T22:37:49-07:00","id":1487696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487680#post1487680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if you try that bullshit, you better be expected to have plans to stay away for at least a decade or so. Which most vampires won't be willing to risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't vampires supposed to move around every decade or so anyways, if for no other reason than making sure no one notices the lack of aging? Some of the games I have run used this as a mechanic that required the players to rotate which city they were based out of. Theoretically you would have to stay away for at least 40 to 50 years to make sure no one remembers you. So in that time you have changed cities three to six times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T06:32:57-07:00","id":1487724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487696#post1487696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't vampires supposed to move around every decade or so anyways, if for no other reason than making sure no one notices the lack of aging? Some of the games I have run used this as a mechanic that required the players to rotate which city they were based out of. Theoretically you would have to stay away for at least 40 to 50 years to make sure no one remembers you. So in that time you have changed cities three to six times.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that would depend a lot on your unlifestyle. For a Tremere who spends most of their time studying at the Chantry or for a Nosferatu that's hardly an issue. For a social guy probably yes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T11:02:54-07:00","id":1487745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487667#post1487667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[USER=&quot;27369&quot;]This is why I poke at the concept that V:tM lore, traditions, and fluff is more Lost Boys biker gang vampires than vampire power brokers or CEOs. The rules and mechanics just don't connect with business realties after the age of discovery. Once you have colonies or international business groups, those notions of city states kind of fall apart.<br /> <br /> Playing an emo teen vampire drifter, professional assassin, or Lestat style rocker can be cool, but occasionally running a business CEO type can be fun as well. The rules and mechanics just tend to face plant into a brick wall when you start thinking in those terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>While that's partially true, I think you're also bringing it too far.<br /> <br /> First, even irl we face such questions about jurisdiction and residence. Those being simple for most Neonates, but a quagmire for elder vampires whose businesses and interests are spread through many domains just makes sense. It would be weird to have a society with perfectly developed means to deal with internationalization, when the proposal is to have our world made worse, not better.<br /> <br /> Second, for a practical take on this the current system already offers the means to deal with it, as you can have direct deals with official vampire authorities in each city and ease things through Prestation. You have plenty of ways to deal with assets spread through multiple Domains as long as we assume that most actors in this situation are reasonable negotiators for their own good.<br /> <br /> Third, this question of yours completely disregard the distinction between asset management and civil rights. Even Musk, Gates, Bezos and other big company owners can't simply call themselves &quot;world citizens&quot; from the perspective of the law. They have a set residence and need visas to wander around like everyone else, their residence defines access to voting rights and obligation to taxes and all other civil rights and obligations that are tied to the region, and that vary across countries. While it doesn't means they can't have the benefits from more than one area, it does means they're still as dependent on the local laws and authorities of those areas as anyone else.<br /> <br /> And fourth, you're making broad statements to justify a specific scenario that doesn't have to abide to those broad statements. Surely if a vampire has business across multiple Domains, they can probably count on the Princes of such Domains acting within reason, they have protection over their assets while they're not there, and upon visiting they can probably count on a very reasonable staying period if not outright invitation to stay if they want.<br /> <br /> But a vampire that effectively lives at a given Domain Embracing outside it to avoid the Prince, then coming back, is someone actively trying to game the technicalities of the system against the Prince. This Prince feeling the vampire is trying to cheat them and forfeiting both lives isn't an unlikely outcome depending on who's the Prince and who's the Sire, and the only thing that may stay on their way in this situation are the specifics of the circumstance, as happens in any limit test for a rule. In the way you proposed this scenario, that's nothing that says this Prince won't be perceived by peers as in their right to execute both.<br /> <br /> Closing this analysis up, Domain among vampires rarely has direct connection to influence or assets. It is about securing your rights of jurisdiction and about where you satisfy your basic needs, food and shelter. It's about stating rules other vampires are expected to abide to and securing your haven and hunting grounds. Nothing in vampire society stops you from having stakes and influence in the Domain of other vampire or in areas no one have a claim for Domain. And most businesses irl work under the assumption that they'll have to adapt to the laws of several places instead of forcing their own laws upon them, so it has nothing to do with anything resembling the law of Domain. While it is true that the game has very poor tools to help with a CEO-style game, or even international crime rings instead of local mafia, it has little to do with the proposed exercise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487162-vampirism-as-a-positive-subverting-the-core-premise-of-vtm?p=1487696#post1487696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren't vampires supposed to move around every decade or so anyways, if for no other reason than making sure no one notices the lack of aging? Some of the games I have run used this as a mechanic that required the players to rotate which city they were based out of. Theoretically you would have to stay away for at least 40 to 50 years to make sure no one remembers you. So in that time you have changed cities three to six times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if most vampires live in little towns with hardly 10.000 inhabitants.<br /> <br /> You can disguise the lack of ageing for longer than that. You would have to be extremely socially engaged with mortal society for that to be a problem to begin with. And in any big city you can move through social groups instead of moving from the whole city for that anyways. It takes an extremely specific kind of vampire to have to move between cities in such a way, maybe someone who can't help but be a local celebrity anywhere they move to.<br /> <br /> And on top of that, it changes nothing about the Princes of those cities wanting to exert their laws and you not having a lot of clout if you just want to use your movements to ignore them. You're probably just managing to become a pariah on many Domains and your reputation as a problematic visitor starting to precede you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T12:10:39-07:00","id":1487758,"title":"","content":"I agree with Monteparnas. Modern cities arent just isolated vampiric feuds. In fact, most princes and primogen of any given region (like a state inside a country or even entire nations) know each other and regularly meet (or send envoys). Such relations are mutually benefitial on several levels, and unreasonable Princes probably wouldnt remain Princes for long.<br /> <br /> That's in fact a good thing, because it actually expands the stories beyond the confines of simple &quot;city states&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T21:22:53-07:00","id":1489996,"title":"","content":"Consider the following. For young vampires, blood becomes an addiction. You need it not just for survival (a few pints a week) but because it's what makes you FEEL again. Your heart, your lunges, your skin, are cold. After feeding you feel warm, orgasmic, more energetic, more alive. Colors return and emotions resurface. Not just physically but to the point of having vibrant memories!<br /> <br /> For elders with larger blood pool...it takes longer. You have watched kin and kith die. You have seen all the culture (music/dance/theatre/games/hunts) you ever knew die and fade away.<br /> <br /> You must accept being an empty vessel, ready to play pretend 24-7 to survive and never be yourself [fuck me I sound like a Toreador]. But what makes an elder an elder is the drive to survive (hooray illiteration).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27517-theran","name":"Theran","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-13T04:13:38-07:00","id":1490011,"title":"","content":"The work &quot;punk&quot; became a catch-all umbrella term for whatever it is you want it to mean. Flipped off your teacher? Punk. Broke off with your girlfriend during her birthday? Punk. Speedran(?) through Dark Souls? That's totally punk dude! Thusly losing its meaning. It's a buzzword.<br /> <br /> Just like the devil horns. It used to belong to us that listen to Heavy Metal music. In more recent times I've seen hip-hop and pop musicians pull that out. I guess it's something that happens to a lot of things that have been around for long enough.<br /> <br /> As to the op: I've never in 20+ yrs have I played a character who is sad about his vampire condition nor have I personally seen anybody play like that. Just like in real life, you come to terms with who/what you are and go about your business. And we do this really quick too; that's session zero stuff for us. Obviously some people enjoy playing like that, but it's not for me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27541,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","user":"HeavyWhiskey","date":". 08-13-2022, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T09:13:55-07:00","id":1520683,"title":"","content":"Ok, leaving the progeny discussion behind a little bit, one of the many things I disagree with V5 is the fall of Sabbath. &quot;A beast I am lest a beast I become&quot;, and for what I remember, the Sabbath is perfectly ok to accept they have a beast howling inside them and keeping it satisfied is the best way to go. No sun? Ok, lets play in the darkness with our friends Lasombra and Kyasid. Pale, static appearance? Tzimisce and Volguirre can give you a hand. In a general way, there's many things that may bother the Sabbath, but being a vampire is not one of them. But, beyond the traditionally alien philosophy of the Sabbath, there are ways that the vampire may accept themselves as a great and wonderful creature, a top predator (I know, I know) and dance la danse macabre for a long time. It would demand some detachment and self-love, but can be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}